            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic accuracy of dobutamine-atropine stress echocardiography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>407-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To analyze the diagnostic accuracy of dobutamine-atropine stress echocardiography.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We studied 304 consecutive patients using dobutamine-atropine stress echocardiography who underwent coronary angiography within a month of the exam. Patients received high dobutamine doses associated or not with atropine.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The global sensitivity was 92%, specificity was 72% and diagnostic accuracy was 87%. Analyzing 120 patients with normal LV function, we found sensitivity of 85%, specificity of 79% and accuracy of 82%.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Dobutamine-atropine stress echocardiography is an accurate method for the detection of coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
